1.SORT 0S, 1S AND 2S
Given an array arr[] containing only 0s, 1s, and 2s. Sort the array in ascending order.
Note: You need to solve this problem without utilizing the built-in sort function.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public void sort012(int[] arr) {
                int j=0;
                int n=arr.length;
                for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
                    if(arr[i]==0){
                        int temp=arr[i];
                        arr[i]=arr[j];
                        arr[j]=temp;
                        j++;
                    }
                }
                for(int i=j;i<n;i++){
                    if(arr[i]==1){
                        int temp=arr[i];
                        arr[i]=arr[j];
                        arr[j]=temp;
                        j++;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
