2. COUNT ODD EVEN 
Given an array arr[]. The task is to find the number of odd and even elements in the array.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public static void countOddEven(Integer arr[]) {
                int even=0,odd=0;
                for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
                    if(arr[i]%2==0){
                        even++;
                    }else{
                        odd++;
                    }
                }
                System.out.println(odd+" "+even);
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/count-odd-even-java/1


3. SWAP KTH ELEMENTS
Given an array arr[], swap the kth element from the beginning with the kth element from the end.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public void swapKth(List<Integer> arr, int k) {
                int temp=arr.get(k-1);
                arr.set(k-1,arr.get(arr.size()-k));
                arr.set(arr.size()-k,temp);
            }
        }
